---
import { render } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { getTeam } from '../lib/content';

const team = await getTeam();
const bios = await Promise.all(
  team.map(async (member) => ({ member, Content: (await render(member)).Content })),
);
---

<BaseLayout title="Home">
  <section class="band hero">
    <div class="container hero__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Mobile and web applications</p>
      <h1>{site.tagline}</h1>
      <p class="hero__lede">{site.description}</p>
      {/*
        One call to action. There were three, plus a band below repeating this
        one, plus a second form -- four ways to say the same thing, which is
        four chances to pick none of them. /contact is still in the footer for
        anyone who just wants an email address.
      */}
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button" href="/build">Tell us what to build</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/*
    The tagline, explained. This sits directly after the hero because "No app
    left behind" is a claim, and a visitor's next thought is "meaning what?".
  */}
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="tagline-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="tagline-heading">What “no app left behind” means</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Most software does not fail at launch. It fails two years later, when
          the developer has moved on, the platform has shifted underneath it,
          and nobody left in the building knows how it works. We built this
          company around the part of the job most shops treat as an
          afterthought: the updates, the monitoring, the small fixes that keep
          an application worth having.
        </p>
        <p>
          When we build something, we plan for the years after release — who
          maintains it, what it costs to keep current, and what happens when the
          operating system changes out from under it. And if someone else built
          your app and walked away, bring it to us anyway. Orphaned software is
          half the reason we exist.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/*
    Four offerings as a description list rather than prose: each is a term and
    its explanation, and a reader scanning for "do they do the thing I need"
    should be able to find it without reading paragraphs.
  */}
  <section class="section section--subtle" aria-labelledby="build-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="build-heading">What we build</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="offer">
        <div class="offer__item">
          <dt>Mobile apps.</dt>
          <dd>
            iOS and Android, designed around the people who will actually use
            them — not around a feature list.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="offer__item">
          <dt>Web platforms.</dt>
          <dd>
            The portals, dashboards, and admin tools that do the real work
            behind an app, or stand on their own.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="offer__item">
          <dt>The systems underneath.</dt>
          <dd>
            Accounts, payments, notifications, reporting. The plumbing nobody
            notices until it leaks. We build it so it does not.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="offer__item">
          <dt>Rescues.</dt>
          <dd>
            Applications that were built, shipped, and abandoned. We read the
            code, tell you honestly what shape it is in, and either bring it
            back or tell you it is kinder to start over.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="how-heading">How we work</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="offer offer--wide">
        <div class="offer__item">
          <dt>We start with the problem, not the app.</dt>
          <dd>
            Sometimes the answer is software. Sometimes it is a spreadsheet and
            a better process. We will tell you which one you have before you
            spend money finding out.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="offer__item">
          <dt>We scope honestly.</dt>
          <dd>
            You get a plain-language read on what it will take, what it will
            cost, and where the risk lives — before you commit to anything.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="offer__item">
          <dt>We show you working software early.</dt>
          <dd>
            Small releases you can put in front of real users, not a big reveal
            at the end.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="offer__item">
          <dt>We stay.</dt>
          <dd>
            Release day is the middle of the story, not the end. Maintenance,
            monitoring, and updates are part of the plan from day one, priced
            and written down.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    bios.length > 0 && (
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="founders-heading">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-head">
            <h2 id="founders-heading">Who we are</h2>
            <p class="founders__intro">
              Between us: two decades of nonprofit funding and operations, and
              two decades of building and delivering software for defense and
              intelligence missions. We have both spent our careers in rooms
              where the work had to actually work — which is the standard we
              hold our software to.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="team">
            {bios.map(({ member, Content }) => (
              <article class="team__member">
                {member.data.image && (
                  /* alt="" on purpose: the name sits right beside it, so
                     describing the photo would just repeat that name. */
                  <img
                    class="team__photo"
                    src={member.data.image}
                    alt=""
                    width="120"
                    height="120"
                    loading="lazy"
                    decoding="async"
                  />
                )}
                <h3>{member.data.name}</h3>
                <p class="team__role">{member.data.role}</p>
                <p class="muted team__summary">{member.data.summary}</p>
                <div class="prose team__bio">
                  <Content />
                </div>
              </article>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    )
  }
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  /* `.container` sets max-width:72rem AND margin-inline:auto. Narrowing this
     box to the text measure therefore centred it, leaving the hero copy adrift
     of the header logo. Keep the box at container width so its left edge lines
     up, and hold the measure on the children instead. */
  .hero__inner {
    max-width: var(--container);
  }

  .hero__inner > * {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .hero__lede {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: #cfe0f7;
  }

  /* Term and description on one line at width, stacked when there is no room
     for two columns. `dt` carries the weight so the list scans as headings. */
  .offer {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(24rem, 100%), 1fr));
  }

  .offer--wide {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .offer__item {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .offer dt {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .offer dd {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .founders__intro {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .team {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(22rem, 100%), 1fr));
  }

  .team__member {
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
  }

  .team__photo {
    width: 120px;
    height: 120px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    margin-block-end: var(--space-md);
    border: 3px solid var(--color-bg);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--color-border);
  }

  .team__member h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .team__role {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-accent-warm);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .team__summary {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .team__bio {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-md);
  }

</style>
